      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T19:03:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem quite right to me but I might be missing something. Chrome creates/uses AHBs with real format like RGBA_8888. It\u0027s just the AHBs created by video decoders that have external format. If we import RGBA_8888 or similar format AHB into Dawn it uses SharedTextureMemory around [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/dawn_ahardwarebuffer_image_representation.cc;l\u003d112;drc\u003d7e9fdfc244e7bb32269d952adce9c54a8380acb1) so wouldn\u0027t that also use SharedTextureMemoryContentsVk? If so we can\u0027t assume format is always OpaqueYCbCrAndroid.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "862f6cf2535a4284ffca9c57d208b621486a42bb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
